From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tyler Smith <74526874+tylertms@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 09:19:06 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(amdgpu): decide PCIe speed switching by the host's
 processor, as Linux does on x86

amdgpu turns PCIe speed switching off on Intel hosts and on Pinnacle
Ridge, under CONFIG_X86, which Stela's build does not set: those hosts
kept the switching Linux turns off there. Stela gives cpu_data the boot
processor's identity from CPUID, so the same code runs.
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
index eaa8340ffbb288833147b4f040a4763cd1036cf7..4c9f8e153c3eb91fa2928b8ee9f814633c55c304 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -1389,7 +1389,10 @@ bool amdgpu_device_seamless_boot_supported(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
  */
 static bool amdgpu_device_pcie_dynamic_switching_supported(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 {
-#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86)
+	/* Stela: its build sets no CONFIG_X86, but it runs on an x86 host and
+	 * gives cpu_data the boot processor's identity from CPUID, so the host
+	 * gets the answer Linux gives it. */
+#if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_X86) || IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_STELA)
 	struct cpuinfo_x86 *c = &cpu_data(0);
 
 	/* eGPU change speeds based on USB4 fabric conditions */
